{
  "pedal": "JOYO R-07 Aquarius (Low Bit mode, mono: Input -> Output)",
  "comment": "First pass on the Low Bit delay. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal. MODE stays on Low Bit throughout; no tap tempo, looper off. Questions: the dry path (digital or analog, any delay); the delay per Time position; the wet's tone; the reduced sample rate (mirror images of the held sine and the sweeps, single clicks dropped or held) and the bit depth (the ladder's repeats: noise against level, the staircase at low levels, the clip at the top); whether the reduction sits before or after Level and inside the feedback loop (repeats crunchier on every pass, or cut off below the last bit). The marker only goes to the loopback: through the pedal its repeat would land on the signal. The ladder and the clicks assume the delay at Time 12:00 lies between 0.25 and 2.75 s (the pedal's longest is said to be ~3.5 s).",
